From: openwrt-rx23302
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] luci-mod-network: wireless page for the vendor driver rtl8192cd

The radios of ELECTRA RX23302 run the vendor driver rtl8192cd (rtl8192fe 3.8.0),
driven by /lib/netifd/wireless/rtl8192cd.sh without hostapd: the driver does
WPA-PSK itself, 802.11ac on the 5 GHz chip, access point mode only.

LuCI only knows mac80211 (features probed from hostapd) and broadcom, so for
hwtype 'rtl8192cd' it offered "No Encryption" as the ONLY choice: opening the
"Edit" dialog of a WPA2 network and pressing "Save" turned it into an open network
(found on the board 05.10.2026). Also no AC mode on 5 GHz, Client/Ad-Hoc modes that
the driver script refuses, a "Join Network" button for them, and "undefined dBm"
for the transmit power the driver does not report.

- encryption: WPA2-PSK / WPA-PSK+WPA2-PSK / WPA-PSK (+ none), ciphers without
  CCMP-256/GCMP (the script knows CCMP and TKIP only);
- frequency: AC mode available for rtl8192cd (11ac is done by the driver);
- mode: access point only, no wpad-mesh hint; no "Join Network" in the scan list;
- status: Tx-Power line hidden when unknown instead of "undefined dBm";
- key: the WPA key field no longer depends on ppsk=0 for rtl8192cd (the PPSK
  flag is removed there, so the field stayed hidden and the password could not
  be changed in LuCI; reported by Sanya 07.10.2026).

v4 (06.10.2026, "show everything the hardware can do"): automatic channel, 20/40
coexistence and forced 40 MHz, required mode N/AC, 802.11b, country (100 codes of the
driver), cell density, beacon interval, RTS/fragmentation, distance, short GI 20/40/80,
LDPC; per network: hidden SSID, WMM, client isolation, bridge isolation, MAC address,
short preamble, DTIM, GTK rekey, inactivity limit, MAC filter (up to 128), WEP
open/shared/both with keys 1-4. PPSK (hostapd + RADIUS) is not offered.
v5: transmit power in percent (txpower_percent -> MIB powerpercent) and 802.11w
(kernel built with CONFIG_RTL_11W_SUPPORT and POWER_PERCENT_ADJUSTMENT).

Other drivers are not affected: every change is under hwtype == 'rtl8192cd'
(and the Tx-Power line only drops a null value).

